A||||4||Jncomutt||Porting intake manifold??  (4 cyl)||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||12-09-2001||07:03 PM||||I just read in the chat that porting the intake in the 4cyl could make for a bit better running.. Well as I don't know much about this, wondering if anyone has any info on it.  Perhaps a how-to, maybe some before/after pics, any notice in performance??<P>I have a spair intake.  Its off of an 86 but I'm thinking it should be the same for the 84, and I'm willing to play (port) with it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||12-09-2001||10:03 PM||||When I <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010824-2-008608.html" TARGET=_blank>ported the head</A> on my '85 Duke, I also opened the intake manifold a tad to match the intake gasket.  The combination of head and intake porting gained a little high-end push.  I don't know if porting the manifold only would have noticeable effect.<P>Good luck, anyhow!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||ITB 2M4||12-10-2001||02:11 AM||||Anytime you can get more air and fuel into the combustion chamber, it's a good thing.  Porting the intake manifold only would mean less time for the intake runners of the head to become 'charged' with air, but the head would only move the same amount of air as it had before.  Porting the head as well will make a noticeable improvement.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||14
Z||000003||fotofrank||12-10-2001||01:23 PM||||Porting and matching the intake and exhaust manifolds to the head will incress top end preformance. However low end torq and HP will decress. The Duke intake and exhaust maifolds are not as restritive as the V6 is.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE||||reg||11
Z||000004||MODIFIE||12-10-2001||03:19 PM||||If you port match the head to header gasket and go 1/16 smaller from the head to intake it will make like a turbo effect and pull more air in and it will improve performance. this was done to my dads 67 mustange fast back 2+2 with a 302 that would pull the front wheels all the 2nd gear and got 21mpg if he kept his foot out of the 4B.||||reg||12
